  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that vortioxetine may interact with the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2 through a multi-step pathway. The drug is known to target the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit beta-2, which in turn is a target of ABT-560 and of another compound, (3S,4aS,8aR)-5,8a-dimethyl-3-prop-1-en-2-yl-2,3,4,4a,7,8-hexahydro-1H-naphthalene. This second compound also targets the Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2, indicating a potential indirect interaction between vortioxetine and this receptor subunit. Additionally, vortioxetine is shown to target Coagulation factor VII, which is also a target of the same compound, further supporting a broader pharmacological pathway. The scores from the different paths suggest a consistent relationship, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains unclear, as the evidence does not specify the direct interaction between vortioxetine and Gamma-aminobutyric acid receptor subunit gamma-2. The observed scores may reflect the cumulative effect of the drug's interactions through different targets, highlighting the complexity of the pharmacological network.",
